Independent, unofficial research project; maintainer account: zhiyuzhang001-a11y.

BORIS reference and adaptation:
Serban Lepadatu, BORIS computational spintronics framework.
https://github.com/SerbanL/Boris2
Pinned v3.80 commit: 6f55516f46f5b6b6ed92bb030d62abab87b4a2f0.
The unmodified upstream GPLv3 LICENSE is retained as COPYING.
SDesc in src/sdesc.hpp adapts the AFM rational update, alternating BB step
selection and reset/clamp logic in Boris/DiffEqAFM_Evals_SD.cpp. Default
1 fs/1 ns bounds and A-pre-update schedule semantics were traced through
Boris/DiffEq_CommonBase_Control.cpp, DiffEq_Defs.h and SimSchedule.cpp.
Changes from BORIS: standalone C++ data structures, two own-Ms spin arrays,
fixed model assembly, binary checkpoint/control serialization and diagnostic
output. This is not upstream source compatibility or installation equivalence.
Scientific reference: Lepadatu, J. Appl. Phys. 128, 243902 (2020),
DOI 10.1063/5.0024382; Exl et al., DOI 10.1063/1.4862839.

Demagnetization:
FM Newell primitives were implemented from the mathematical equations;
Newell, Williams and Dunlop (1993), DOI 10.1029/93JB00694.
The Gaussian fixed-eight reference is a separate project implementation
using surface charges and directed MPFR intervals, not a Newell reuse.
The frozen FiM kernel is project-generated numerical data. Historical
production construction used BORIS/OOMMF-derived asymptotic routines;
BORIS DemagTFunc_Asympt.cpp credits M. J. Donahue / OOMMF for the
asymptotic equations. That upstream chain is acknowledged here. The optional user-workflow kernel builder now bundles only the minimal
DemagTFunc_Asympt.cpp/.h extract under src/user_kernel, retaining its credit
and this GPLv3 license chain. Private archives and upstream source trees are
not bundled.
The kernel itself is a finite-mirror dataset, not infinite-PBC certification.

